# Notice

## This is fiction

Everything under `kb/`, and every note in the encrypted release asset, is
original fiction written for this repository. It is a character sketch of a
fictional politician with poor judgement, used as demo data. Any resemblance to a
real person, company, government or event is coincidental.

`Zaphod Beeblebrox` is used here as the name of a lab test fixture — the same
name the lab's burned key vector has carried for years. This repository is not
affiliated with, endorsed by, or derived from any published work, and reproduces
no text from one. Nothing here is an adaptation, a sequel or a quotation.

`ACME Corporation` is used as a generic fictional company name. The memos, terms
and minutes are original inventions; they describe no real transaction.

## No warranty, no secrets

The keys are burned, the notes are jokes, the workflows are exercises. Nothing in
this repository is a credential you can use, and nothing in the encrypted notes is
confidential — decrypting them requires a key that is published here, which makes
